  "name": "NMDA RECEPTOR ANTIBODY (NR1)",
  "code": "2818",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>1. Auto Immune reactivity are not by themselves diagnostic and must be correlated with other laboratory and clinical<br>findings.<br>2. Test conducted on 1:10 diluted serum.<br>3. Antigen substrate - transfected cells of EU-90.<br>4. Testing serum and CSF both are recommended, as in most patients intrathecal synthesis of anti-glutamate receptor (type NMDA) antibodies is seen.</p>\n<p><strong>Comments</strong></p>\n<p>Auto antibodies against glutamate receptors (NMDA type) are specific markers for anti glutamate receptor type encephalitis.<br>This is an inflammatory encephalopathic autoimmune disease and still widely under diagnosed. This is frequently associated&nbsp;with ovarian and testicular teratoma</p>",
